<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lop Nur</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Lop Nor</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lop Nur is a former salt lake, now largely dry, in the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarim-basin">Tarim Basin</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xinjiang">Xinjiang</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. The ancient oasis kingdom of Kroraina, called Loulan in Chinese, lay on its north-western shore, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk-road">Silk Road</a> between China and the western oases. Changes in the course of the Tarim River shifted and shrank the lake. From 1964 the area was China's nuclear test site.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lop-nur.jpg" alt="Lop Nur" width="320" height="208" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NASA. Image courtesy of Earth Sciences and Image Analysis Laboratory, NASA Johnson Space Center. Color adjusting of t... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Basin_of_Lop_Nur_90.25E,_40.10N,_Desert_of_Lop,_Kum_Tagh_and_Astin_Tagh.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
